<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahadur Shah II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">deposed <a href="/years/1857">1857</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Bahadur Shah Zafar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bahadur Shah II, also known as Bahadur Shah Zafar, was the last Mughal emperor, whose authority by then barely extended beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-rebellion-of-1857">Indian Rebellion of 1857</a> the rebels proclaimed him their leader. After the rebellion's defeat the British deposed him in 1857 and exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a>, formally ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bahadur-shah-ii.jpg" alt="Bahadur Shah II" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bahadur_Shah_II_of_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
